0†06:31†www.youtube.com ) Putting PM, design, and eng bots in the same room\nL50: \nL51:   * (cite11†10:07†www.youtube.com ) A bot that turns photos into dioramas on Peng’s website\nL52: \nL53:   * (cite12†14:16†www.youtube.com ) How Lauren’s bots test their own work before merging\nL54:   * (cite13†17:59†www.youtube.com ) Dr. Eggbot, a bot that designs and audits your bots\nL55: \nL56:   * (cite14†21:27†www.youtube.com ) The assistant bot that booked Lauren’s multi-city trip\nL57: \nL58:   * (cite15†25:22†www.youtube.com ) Eng bots that sometimes land PRs before Lauren reads them\nL59: \nL60:   * (cite16†38:59†www.youtube.com ) How to trust your bots with more work, one skill at a time\nL61: \nL62: * * *\nL63: \nL64: I’m proud to partner with cite17†Granola†www.granola.ai L65: The world’s best teams, including Ramp, Linear, Replit, Brex, and more, use Granola to take notes and focus more in meetings. I’ve tried many meeting apps myself but keep coming back to Granola. It literally helps you take time back in your day.\nL66: \nL67: cite17†Try Granola for Free†www.granola.ai L68: \nL69: * * *\nL70: ## Top takeaways I learned from this episode\nL71: ### How the Grok Bot team uses Grok Bot\nL72: \nL73:   1. Build the design system and one keyframe, then let your design bot scale it. Peng’s design bot connects to Figma through cite18†Figma MCP†developers.figma.com and uses a skill that describes how his files are set up, plus his design system’s colors, type, and spacing. “I will do the first 5%,” Peng said. He builds the system and one keyframe, then asks the bot to extend it into every screen of the flow.\nL74:   2. Make an eng lead bot to manage your other eng bots. Lauren hands big projects to her eng lead bot, Matcha. Matcha doesn’t do work itself. Instead, it breaks down the project for other eng bots to execute on. Each eng bot then spins up coding agents in the cloud, letting Lauren run “really massive agent swarms.”\nL75: ## This post is for paid subscribers\nL76: \nL77: cite19†Already a paid subscriber? Sign in†substack.com L78: \nL79: © 2026 Peter Yang · cite20†Privacy†substack.com ∙ cite21†Terms†substack.com ∙ cite22†Collection notice†substack.com L80: \nL81: cite23†Start your Substack†substack.com cite24†Get the app†substack.com L82: \nL83: cite25†Substack†substack.com is the home for great culture\nL84: \nL85: cite26†Image†analytics.twitter.com cite27†Image†t.co "
